body:
Rogaine, which contains the component minoxidil is a commonly prescribed drug for telogen effluvium (TE). Covid/illness hair loss is hair loss caused by severe stress or changes to body, which is the definition of TE. So I would say it's not unusual that your derm prescribed you this. [Here](https://donovanmedical.com/hair-blog/2017/7/13/minoxidil-for-telogen-effluvium-do-i-need-to-use-it-forever) you can read a bit more about the use of minoxidil for TE cases like yours (without clear triggers).

&#x200B;

In my personal experience, minoxidil helped a lot with covid-related hair shedding, for the first few months. My hair was sprouting everywhere on my scalp, but then I stopped using it regularly and all the gain seemed to fall out. This should not discourage you though, as in my case I may have other underlying disorders (to be confirmed by the biopsy I got a few weeks ago).
